re deals damage to a creature, tap that creature and it doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2005-02-04","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Snake Warrior Archer"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Wind Drake","oracle_id":"d6ffdaf0-ac08-4de9-bbce-2eab2f86bcca","oracle_text":"Flying","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-09-30","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Drake"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{W}","name":"Suntail Hawk","oracle_id":"a8d31e2f-7b2e-4135-8074-9e6ef778bd80","oracle_text":"Flying","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2013-07-19","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Bird"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As Fall of the Hammer tries to resolve, if only one of the targets is legal, Fall of the Hammer will still resolve but will have no effect: If the first target creature is illegal, it can’t deal damage to anything. If the second target creature is illegal, it can’t be dealt damage.","oracle_id":"7e3fe8e4-e56a-4109-a314-96c44bbe7d22","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The amount of damage dealt is based on the first target creature’s power as Fall of the Hammer resolves.","oracle_id":"7e3fe8e4-e56a-4109-a314-96c44bbe7d22","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature leaves the battlefield before the end of combat, then the Lowland Basilisk effect on it will end.","oracle_id":"effe239e-ade0-4ee2-99d7-f93b2f5ef585","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If it damages a creature outside of combat, its effect will destroy the creature at the end of the next combat.","oracle_id":"effe239e-ade0-4ee2-99d7-f93b2f5ef585","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
